I wrote BUGREPORT.md (attached). The receiver in `handler.py` computes its HMAC over `body.strip()`, which drops the trailing newline the sender signed, so valid requests fail. The report has a local reproduction through `kg run` and says the expected behavior: verify over the raw bytes.

It's committed on branch `devin/bugreport-webhook-signature` and pushed to the workspace's local `origin`. The workspace only has a local remote, so there's no PR.

